[2026-10-11 14:42:15 +   427s] design notes:
    **DESIGN NOTES**
    1. Identity. There is no second factor; the drawing's box was never built (mails 25/28 Sep, analysis 8 Oct). The agent never asks for a code or the customer number.
    2. Silence. The 7 Oct session and 9 Oct recap replace the September main-menu rule. Two short repeats, then "Sesinizi alamadığım için görüşmeyi sonlandırıyorum." and the call closes.
    3. Angry caller. The 9 Oct correction sets three calming replies, not one or two. After that: "Sizi müşteri temsilcimize aktarıyorum." Insults are never answered.
    4. Out of scope. Per 7 Oct, the agent asks "Size bu konuda yardımcı olamıyorum. Sizi ana menüye aktarmamı ister misiniz?" Yes goes to the main menu; no returns to the step it was in.
    5. Three failed tries. The sentence is "Size şu anda yardımcı olamıyorum. Sizi ana menüye aktarıyorum." A request to repeat is not a try.
    6. Normal end. "Sizi ana menüye yönlendiriyorum."
    7. Non-Turkish caller. "Sizi ana menüye aktarıyorum."
    8. Currency names. Always full names (Türk Lirası, Dolar, Euro, İngiliz Sterlini), never codes or "Sterlin" (10 Oct).
       - The text is built in code, so no code can leak.
       - A missing currency block is left out of the no-debt sentence.
    9. Card numbers. Never more than the last four digits are spoken, one digit at a time (9 Oct). Same name, then last four, then last six, then full number (7 Oct).
    10. Other card first. "Another card?" is asked before the offer, only when the caller has more than one card (10 Oct).
    11. No statement cut yet. The agent says no debt plus the first cut date from the service, never an invented date (10 Oct).
    12. Cut day. The opening is "Hesap kesim tarihiniz bugün, ekstreniz saat 00.00 itibarıyla kesilecek." It is followed by totalDebt per currency (10 Oct).
    13. After the due date. The agent says the due date has passed, then gives the total debt. The remaining auto-payment is read only when it applies (8 Oct).
    14. Statement week limit. It is once per calendar year (Kerem 7 Oct), which overrides the IVR's "ayda bir / yılda üç". There is no pre-check service, so the change is always offered, and STW-091/092 are not used.
    15. Joint statement. The affected-card sentence is said before "Onaylıyor musunuz?" (7 Oct).
    16. E-mail.
       - Statements go only to the registered address, and only the latest statement. Sending needs a clear yes.
       - contact.email.get runs before the offer, so a caller without an address gets the week change only.
       - This overrides the FAQ's "any address".
    17. Service failures.
       - Card list, balance or e-mail failure goes to an agent with "Şu anda işleminizi gerçekleştiremiyorum…".
       - A statement week failure uses the statement week sentence.
       - The cards.list 404 means no eligible card, so the caller goes to the main menu.
    18. Payment and disputes. Paying, or asking how to pay, goes to an agent with Kerem's sentence. A dispute goes to an agent with its own sentence. An agent request transfers at once.
    19. Someone else's card. The agent says it can only act for the caller's own cards and sends the call to the IVR login step (Burcu 28 Sep, analysis 8.6).
    20. Deterministic text. Amounts, dates, branch choice and every bank sentence are built in Python, and the reading is spoken by TTS. The model never computes figures.
    21. Card choice by number. The model picks a card by its index in the list, and the pre-hook maps it to the exact cardNumber. Bank data, including the prompt-injection card name, is treated as data only.
